WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.880
Drop a small piece of lung into water.

2
00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:04.050
It floats.

3
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:08.470
It is full of air, held in
tiny sacs called alveoli.

4
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.940
A pair of lungs holds
hundreds of millions of them.

5
00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:16.340
Yet the lungs have no muscle of their
own to pull air into those sacs.

6
00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:20.590
So how do your lungs pull air
in, with no muscle of their own?

7
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:24.270
In this mission, you'll follow
the air down the airway tree,

8
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.760
from the trachea to the alveoli.

9
00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:32.180
Then you'll zoom in on one alveolus,
where the wall is just one cell thick.

10
00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:37.490
Your mission: explain how your lungs pull
air in without any muscle of their own.
